      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "For local tasks, install Air in your JetBrains IDE , select GitHub Copilot , and connect your GitHub Copilot account.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-03-github-copilot-is-now-available-in-jetbrains-air",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-03T15:11:46.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-05T18:01:40.263Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "For cloud tasks, you&rsquo;ll need a JetBrains account in an Air Teams-enabled business organization, a GitHub Copilot subscription, and Copilot enabled by your Air administrator.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-03-github-copilot-is-now-available-in-jetbrains-air",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-03T15:11:46.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-05T18:01:40.263Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "When you run a GitHub Copilot cloud task through JetBrains Air, Copilot works in a Docker container on a fresh virtual machine.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-03-github-copilot-is-now-available-in-jetbrains-air",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-03T15:11:46.000Z",
